{"id": "EUVD-2026-104303", "enisaUuid": "5a270a93-8f59-36c8-a908-6c053bc03524", "description": "SGLang through 0.5.22 with the Mooncake disaggregation backend contains an uncontrolled memory allocation vulnerability in handle_staging_rsp() that lets unauthenticated network-adjacent attackers exhaust Prefill memory. Attackers can obtain the rank address from the /route endpoint and send STAGING_RSP messages with huge chunk_idx values under fresh room IDs, causing the scheduler to be OOM-killed.", "datePublished": "2026-10-19T13:55:18", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T16:34:55", "baseScore": 7.1, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:A/AC:L/AT:N/PR:N/UI:N/VC:N/VI:N/VA:H/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/issues/45014", "https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/blob/v0.5.22/python/sglang/srt/disaggregation/common/staging_handler.py#L505-L548", "https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/blob/v0.5.22/python/sglang/srt/disaggregation/mooncake/conn.py#L2885-L2935", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/sglang-through-0.5.22-memory-exhaustion-via-mooncake-staging-rsp-chunk-idx"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-112270", "GHSA-q322-x26r-gm37"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.25, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "de5d9a93-a979-3319-95e7-31da9c2a0441", "product": {"name": "sglang", "vendor": {"name": "sgl-project"}}, "product_version": "0 \u22640.5.22"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "e43e2e66-d63f-379b-a7f7-70d614a8462a", "vendor": {"name": "sgl-project"}}], "isExploited": false}